# /opt/elimelec/caddy/Caddyfile - the front door. One block per
# environment; Odoo answers on 8069, its live connection (the bell, the
# task toasts) on 8072 under /websocket. Odoo's own login is the only
# gate on the three environments (owner, 11/10/2026); the basic-auth
# gate below protects the overview page's action buttons only. Its
# password hash is filled in on the server (caddy hash-password).
(gate) {
	basic_auth {
		elimelec GATE_PASSWORD_HASH
	}
}

(odoo) {
	encode zstd gzip
	request_body {
		max_size 128MB
	}
	reverse_proxy /websocket* {args[0]}:8072
	reverse_proxy {args[0]}:8069
}

elimelecodoo.com {
	# the client's UAT page and its tick-offs (owner, 12/10/2026):
	# static files under /opt/elimelec/uat, results kept by
	# bin/uat-server.py on :8071 (systemd elimelec-uat)
	redir /uat /uat/ 308
	handle /uat/api/* {
		reverse_proxy host.docker.internal:8071
	}
	handle_path /uat/* {
		root * /srv/uat
		file_server
		header Cache-Control "no-store"
	}
	handle {
		import odoo prod-odoo
	}
}

www.elimelecodoo.com {
	redir https://elimelecodoo.com{uri} permanent
}

staging.elimelecodoo.com {
	import odoo staging-odoo
}

dev.elimelecodoo.com {
	import odoo dev-odoo
}

# the overview page, open to read (owner's choice): no client data on it.
# Its buttons post to /actions/*, which the gate protects and the action
# service on the host answers (deploy/server/bin/actions-server.py).
status.elimelecodoo.com {
	handle /actions/* {
		import gate
		reverse_proxy host.docker.internal:8070 {
			flush_interval -1
		}
	}
	handle {
		root * /srv/status
		file_server
		header Cache-Control "no-store"
	}
}
